<style>@page{size:A4;margin:10mm}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{font:11.2px/1.32 Arial,sans-serif;color:#17242e;margin:0}h1{font-size:23px;margin:0 0 4px}header{border-bottom:3px solid #17242e;padding-bottom:9px;margin-bottom:10px}.meta{font-size:10px;color:#52616c}.notice{background:#fff0d3;border-left:4px solid #bf7414;padding:9px 11px}.notice strong{display:block;font-size:12px;margin-bottom:4px}h2{font-size:13px;margin:11px 0 5px;padding-bottom:4px;border-bottom:1px solid #bac4cb}p{margin:5px 0 6px}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:10.5px;margin:5px 0}td,th{text-align:left;padding:5px 6px;border-bottom:1px solid #d8dfe3}th{background:#edf1f4}td:nth-child(2){text-align:center;white-space:nowrap}code{font:10.1px Consolas,monospace}ul.parts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;column-gap:20px;row-gap:3px;list-style:none;padding:0;margin:6px 0}.parts li{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;border-bottom:1px dotted #d0d8dd;padding:3px 0}.parts b{font-size:10px;white-space:nowrap}.optional{background:#edf2f5;padding:7px 9px;margin-top:7px}ol,ul.notes{padding-left:18px;margin:5px 0}li{margin:3px 0}footer{border-top:1px solid #a8b4bd;margin-top:10px;padding-top:6px;font-size:9.5px;color:#495a65}section{break-inside:avoid}</style></head><body>
<header><h1>KITTY V7.1 · FRONT + REAR ultrasonic</h1><div class="meta">TEAM PROMETHEUS · 24 OCTOBER 2026 (IST) · REPLACES THE EARLIER V7 SHOP ORDER</div></header>
<div class="notice"><strong>PRINT THE FIT STAGE FIRST — PHYSICAL FIT IS PENDING</strong>Both front and rear HC-SR04 mounts are included. The rear bracket is a separate, replaceable part using existing chassis bolts. Use the actual motors, wheels, sensors, phone/case and fasteners for fit checks before large covers.</div>
<section><h2>1 / First order — seven pieces</h2><table><tr><th>Files</th><th>Quantity</th><th>Check</th></tr>
<tr><td><code>FIT_TEST_FIRST/</code> — all five STL files</td><td>1 each / 5 total</td><td>Tail key/socket, phone thickness, M3 holes and new rear-sensor face</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>ROBOT_PARTS/v7_motor_left.stl</code></td><td>1</td><td>Actual motor, shaft, ties and fasteners</td></tr>
<tr><td><code>ROBOT_PARTS/v7_rear_sensor_bracket.stl</code></td><td>1</td><td>Actual rear module, header, cable exit and tie retention</td></tr></table>
<p><b>The left motor holder and rear bracket count toward the 13 production parts below; keep them if they fit and do not print them twice.</b> Use the intended production printer/material/profile. Match gauge and mating-part print directions and support removal. Current tail gap: 0.4 mm per side; M3 holes: 3.4 mm. Request a CAD correction if fit fails; do not scale whole parts.</p></section>
<section><h2>2 / Production — 13 separate robot parts total</h2><p>Folder: <code>ROBOT_PARTS/</code>. Quantity <b>one of each</b>, including the two retained stage-1 parts.</p><ul class="parts">__PART_LIST__</ul>
<div class="optional"><b>OPTIONAL — quantity 0:</b> <code>OPTIONAL_DO_NOT_PRINT/v7_battery_tray.stl</code>. Internal tray included for future use; an external AA holder/restraint is still unselected.</div></section>
<section><h2>3 / Rear sensor installation and service access</h2><ol>
<li>Test the actual HC-SR04 in the rear face gauge. Assumed PCB: <b>45 × 20 × 1.6 mm</b>; transducers: <b>16 mm diameter, 26 mm centres</b>; printed openings: <b>17.6 mm</b>. Actual module variations require this fit check.</li>
<li>Fit the rear module to the <b>detached bracket first</b>: cans point outward/rearward, lower PCB corners rest on the saddles, header exits through the centre notch. Retain with two ties through the side slots; keep the can faces clear and avoid pressure on components.</li>
<li>Install the bridge <b>under the chassis</b> through its two existing rear cover/base M3 holes. Allow <b>3 mm extra bolt grip</b> plus the real washer stack; verify screw length, nut engagement and ground clearance. Route and secure the cable using the post eye and existing service opening, clear of tyres and tail.</li>
<li>The rear sensor is offset beside the tail. Both rear openings, KITTY lettering and tail removal remain accessible in the CAD checks. Remove the two bracket bolts for bench servicing; do not lift the robot by this bracket or tail.</li></ol></section>
<section><h2>4 / Printing and remaining fit checks</h2><ul class="notes">
<li><b>Millimetres, 100% scale; separate objects.</b> The new bracket and rear face gauge have stable upright bases in their supplied axes; use matching orientations and supports at hole roofs/notches. Review covers’ internal roofs and all support removal in the slicer.</li>
<li><b>Suggested FDM quote:</b> PETG, 0.2 mm layers, 4–5 walls, about 35% infill / 50% for structural mounts and neck. Shop-specific settings, tolerances and strength need confirmation. Preserve holes, slots, raised PROMETHEUS/KITTY letters and tail keyway.</li>
<li>Motor reservation: <b>65 × 24 × 20 mm</b> plus clearance; ±2 mm fore/aft slots. Wheel outside diameter: <b>62.5 mm</b>; shaft/hub/axial width and caster contact remain unverified. Phone report: <b>164 × 76 × 8 mm</b>; check full case, camera, buttons and cable access.</li>
</ul></section>
<footer><b>Order:</b> 5 gauges + 13 production pieces; optional tray excluded. Actual sensors, wheels, motors, phone, caster and electronics are purchased items, not print parts. Source geometry/meshes and sampled clearances passed; physical fit, load capacity and real sensor coverage remain unverified. IR mounting is not included. Fit-stage results must be checked before large parts.</footer>
</body></html>
